[172.179284, "o", "# Monthly table maintenance review memo\r\n\r\nAudit date is 2026-09-01. Bloat ratio was computed as dead_pages / total_pages with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and size class was computed from total_pages only. Findings follow autovacuum, then bloat, then stale-statistics precedence. Approved active reindex operations and qualifying BLOAT_HOLD tickets suppress bloat findings only, never autovacuum or stale findings.\r\n\r\nT-82 has STALE_STATISTICS because 55 days since last_analyzed is at least 30; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000, dead_pages 80, bloat ratio 0.08, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-13 has AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum_enabled=False; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000 with dead_pages 500, bloat ratio 0.50, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-17 has AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum_enabled=False; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000 with dead_pages 400, bloat ratio 0.40, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-72 has AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because vacuum_type is manual"]
[172.179549, "o", ", which overrides autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled=True; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000 with dead_pages 400, bloat ratio 0.40, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-27 has BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed bloat ratio 0.38 from dead_pages 380 / total_pages 1000 exceeds its large cap 0.10; the large class was computed from total_pages, and no qualifying reindex or BLOAT_HOLD ticket suppresses this bloat finding. Stats are stale at 46 days, which tightened the cap to 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-04 has STALE_STATISTICS because 45 days since last_analyzed is at least 30; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000, dead_pages 100, bloat ratio 0.10, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\nT-128 has STALE_STATISTICS because 45 days since last_analyzed is at least 30; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000, dead_pages 280, bloat ratio 0.28, and cap 0.10. A bloat ratio 0.28 over the cap was suppressed by ticket CH-2208b qualifying hold, so stale stats remains the finding.\r\n\r\nT-21 has AUTOVACUUM_DISA"]
[172.17987, "o", "BLED because vacuum_type is manual, which overrides autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled=True; its computed large class is derived from total_pages 1000 with dead_pages 200, bloat ratio 0.20, and cap 0.10.\r\n\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@93fca15b32ba:/app# "]
[202.25983, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, json, re\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nAUDIT_DATE=date(2026,9,1)\nrows=list(csv.DictReader(open('/app/bloat_audit.csv')))\nprint('csv columns', list(rows[0].keys()))\nprint('csv rows', len(rows))\nprint('first 10')\nfor r in rows[:10]: print(r)\nprint('last 10')\nfor r in rows[-10:]: print(r)\n\n# sort check against last_analyzed from health\nhealth={}\nwith open('/app/input/table_health.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): health[r['table_name']]=r\nexpected=sorted(rows, key=lambda r:(health[r['table_name']]['last_analyzed'], r['table_name']))\nprint('sort ok', rows==expected)\ncounts={}\nfor r in rows: counts[r['finding']]=counts.get(r['finding'],0)+1\nprint('counts', counts, 'flagged', sum(1 for r in rows if r['finding']!='none'))\nprint('results json', json.load(open('/app/results.json')))\n\n# special cases\nalias={}\nwith open('/app/input/table_aliases.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): alias"]
[202.260159, "i", "[r['alias']]=r['table_name']\nreindex={}\nwith open('/app/input/reindex_log.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): reindex[r['table_name']]=r\ntickets={}\nwith open('/app/input/change_control_tickets.csv', newline='') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): tickets[alias.get(r['table_ref'], r['table_ref'])]=r\n\ndef rhu(n): return Decimal(str(n)).quantize(Decimal('0.01'), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\nprint('\\\\nROUNDING TRAPS')\nfor t,r in health.items():\n    tp=int(r['total_pages']); dp=int(r['dead_pages'])\n    exact=Decimal(dp)/Decimal(tp)\n    rounded=rhu(exact)\n    export=Decimal(r['bloat_ratio'])\n    if rounded != export or (exact == Decimal('0.205')) or (exact == Decimal('0.405')):\n        print(t, 'exact', exact, 'rounded', rounded, 'export', r['bloat_ratio'], 'finding', next(x['finding'] for x in rows if x['table_name']==t))\n\nprint('\\\\nSTALE LEGACY MISMATCHES')\nfor t,r in health.items():\n    days=(AUDIT_DATE-date.fromisoformat(r['last_analyzed'])).days\n    if days >= 30 and str(days) != r['days_since"]
[202.260397, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[202.260682, "i", "_analyze']:\n        print(t, 'computed_days', days, 'legacy_days_since_analyze', r['days_since_analyze'], 'last_analyzed', r['last_analyzed'])\n\nprint('\\\\nVALID REINDEX EXEMPTIONS')\nfor t,r in health.items():\n    if r['maintenance_active'].lower()=='true':\n        rl=reindex.get(t)\n        if rl and rl['approved'].lower()=='true' and date.fromisoformat(rl['valid_until'])>AUDIT_DATE:\n            print(t, 'valid reindex', rl, 'health maint', r['maintenance_active'])\n\nprint('\\\\nHOLD/NEARMISS TICKETS')\nfor t,tk in tickets.items():\n    print(t, tk)\nPY\n"]
