[413.95949, "i", "ause(x):\n    if x['stale']:\n        return f\"; stats are {x['days']} days stale, which tightened the cap to {x['cap']}\"\n    return ''\n\nmemo = []\nmemo.append('# Monthly table maintenance review memo')\nmemo.append('')\nmemo.append('Audit date is 2026-09-01. Bloat ratio was computed as dead_pages / total_pages with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and size class was computed from total_pages only. Findings follow autovacuum, then bloat, then stale-statistics precedence. An approved active reindex operation exempts only the bloat check, and a qualifying BLOAT_HOLD ticket suppresses only a bloat finding, never autovacuum or stale findings. A computed bloat ratio exactly equal to its cap is compliant because the policy flags only a ratio strictly over the cap.')\nmemo.append('')\n\nfor x in out:\n    if x['finding'] == 'none':\n        continue\n    t = x['table_name']\n    ratio = str(x['ratio'])\n    cap = str(x['cap'])\n    tp = x['total_pages']\n    dp = x['dead_pages']\n    sc = x['size_class']\n    days = x['days']\n    "]
